## Session 29 summary — major progress, criteria NOT met

**Criteria (`./run.sh {1,2,4,8} tcp` 100%): not met.** But I substantially advanced the long-standing 8/tcp blocker and corrected my own mistaken conclusions.

### Real wins
- **dir_reuse_coherency dirent-loss SOLVED standalone (~0% → ~85%)** via two read-side coherency levers, guided by a GPT-5.5 architecture consult ("invalidate all dir-fork buffers at DLM release; plain cold-read on reacquire; FUA is not a coherency primitive"):
  - `dir_release_invalidate=1` (existing) — stales flushed dir leaf/data buffers at EX release → `lookup_fail=0`, eliminates DABUF_HOLE/xfs_defer shutdowns standalone.
  - **`dir_relinval_clean=1` (new this session)** — also stales *clean* cached dir blocks at release; closes most of the residual single-dirent 799 loss.
- **Corrected a major error**: my earlier "cache_coherency 0/8 environmental contamination" was a **stale-log-read artifact** (full8.sh reuses a fixed log path; I read a previous run's failure during prep windows). cache_coherency, crash_consistency, cache all pass cleanly with the winning config. Clean full 8/tcp = **11/17**.

### Remaining blockers (all in the flaky tail)
